---
import AppLayout from '../../../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import AppSupport from '../../../components/AppSupport.astro';
import { chatLikeGenZ, appPath, studio } from '../../../data/apps';

const path = appPath(chatLikeGenZ);
const features = [
  ['Encode', 'Turn an ordinary message into three options: Chill, Dry and Hype. Pick the one that sounds like you.'],
  ['Decode', 'Get a plain-language interpretation of unfamiliar slang, with an explanation of the terms.'],
  ['Make it yours', 'Choose a writing style and, if you want, an age range, identity and pronouns to guide new encodes.'],
  ['Keep your balance', 'Start as a guest with 10 conversions. Link Google if you want to recover a saved balance after changing devices.'],
];
---

<AppLayout
  title="Chat Like Gen Z | Writing utility | AppCrazy Labs"
  description="Encode everyday text in three Gen Z-style tones or decode slang into plain language. Learn how Chat Like Gen Z handles credits, conversion text and privacy."
  canonicalPath={path}
  heading={chatLikeGenZ.name}
  kicker="AppCrazy Labs · Writing utility"
  deck={chatLikeGenZ.tagline}
  backLabel={studio.name}
  backHref={studio.path}
>
  <div slot="meta" class="hero-actions">
    <a class="button button-primary" href="#features">Explore the app ↓</a>
    <a class="text-link" href="#support">Get support →</a>
  </div>

  <p>
    Sometimes you know what you mean but want a different way to say it.
    Chat Like Gen Z gives you three versions of your message, or helps you
    understand slang you have come across. You still decide what to send.
  </p>

  <section id="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
    <h2 id="features-title">Two ways to find the words</h2>
    <dl class="app-features">
      {features.map(([name, description]) => (
        <div><dt>{name}</dt><dd>{description}</dd></div>
      ))}
    </dl>
    <p>AI can miss the point, especially with context and slang. Check the result before sharing it.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="credits-title">
    <h2 id="credits-title">A simple conversion balance</h2>
    <p>
      A new guest wallet starts with 10 free conversions. A successful new encode
      or decode uses one conversion. All three encode tones are included; switching
      between them, copying or sharing an existing result does not use another one.
      Failed or cancelled requests return the reserved conversion.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Android test build includes optional rewarded ads intended to add three
      conversions after server verification, and Google Play test purchases of 100,
      200 or 300-conversion packs. Demo ads add no credits. These features are in
      internal testing, not a public offer or live sale.
    </p>
  </section>

  <aside class="note-callout" aria-label="Availability">
    <strong>Currently in internal testing</strong>
    <p>There is no public Google Play download link yet. We will add one when a public listing is available.</p>
  </aside>

  <section aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <h2 id="privacy-title">What happens to your words</h2>
    <p>
      In the current Android wallet build, submitted text goes to our Firebase
      backend and Google Gemini for conversion. Encode also sends the writing
      preferences you selected. Generated results and request metadata are stored
      with your wallet’s conversion records for recovery and credit accounting;
      the app keeps a recent result on your device too. Avoid entering confidential information.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={`${path}privacy/`}>Read the Chat Like Gen Z privacy policy →</a>
      {' '}You can also <a href={`${path}data-deletion/`}>request account and data deletion →</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <AppSupport appName={chatLikeGenZ.name} />
</AppLayout>
